\title{risAT: An R Package Wrapping the API of the Austrian Legal Information System (RIS)}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Search and parse Austrian legal information from the Rechtsinformationssystem (RIS) Open Government Data REST API \url{https://data.bka.gv.at/ris/api/v2.6/} provided by the Austrian Federal Chancellery. Supports case law from all Judikatur applications and consolidated federal law, returning tidy tibbles for reproducible legal research.
}
\details{
risAT uses a two-step request pattern:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Build} a request with \code{\link[=ris_req_case_law]{ris_req_case_law()}}
\item \strong{Perform} it with \code{\link[=ris_perform_case_law]{ris_perform_case_law()}}
}

Convenience wrappers like \code{\link[=ris_search_vwgh]{ris_search_vwgh()}} and \code{\link[=ris_search_vfgh]{ris_search_vfgh()}}
combine both steps for common court applications.
}
